<!--
    Companion to android.hardware.security.keymint-service.default.xml - see that
    file for the full chain. Same failure, second HAL:

        servicemanager: Caller(pid=1386,uid=1000,sid=u:r:recovery:s0) Could not find
        android.hardware.gatekeeper.IGatekeeper/default in the VINTF manifest.

        init: Service 'vendor.gatekeeper_default' (pid 1386) exited with status 1

    keymint alone unwraps the metadata-encryption key, which is what this device's
    metadata_encryption=aes-256-xts:wrappedkey_v0 needs to mount /metadata and read
    the key directory. Gatekeeper is the second half: it verifies the user credential
    and hands back the auth token that gates the per-user key unwrap, so without it
    /data decrypts only as far as the metadata layer and the credential prompt cannot
    succeed. Both are started from init.recovery.qcom.rc and both need a fragment
    here, since servicemanager rejects their addService the same way.
-->
<manifest version="1.0" type="device">
    <hal format="aidl">
        <name>android.hardware.gatekeeper</name>
        <fqname>IGatekeeper/default</fqname>
    </hal>
</manifest>
